            <title>[LU-21174] sanity-sec test_73: name in CREAT changelog record is raw encrypted bytes, not the digested name</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21174</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_73 fails intermittently because the CREAT changelog record of a file in an fscrypt directory carries the raw encrypted name bytes, where the test expects the digested (base64) form that fid2path returns for the locked directory:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  name &amp;lt;binary&amp;gt; in CREAT is not IMT_Mb4xI_N-ZEqs76nvOCBoKd4_3nKpc6V2zW9Hedg&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the failing log the CREAT for the touched file (j=touch.0) and the later RENME (j=mrename.0) both show a binary name, while fid2path gave the digest. The failure is rare (about 0.1% of runs) and spans configurations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same signature (garbage name in CREAT is not &amp;lt;digest&amp;gt;), none linked to a ticket:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-reviews 65094 PS64, review-ldiskfs-arm, 2026-11-10: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/24841099-b743-4d9c-83ec-12a2dedcc753" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/24841099-b743-4d9c-83ec-12a2dedcc753&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-reviews 68233 PS21, review-ldiskfs-ubuntu, 2026-09-10: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8322fd4d-6f92-41a3-958a-593bf0b53015" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8322fd4d-6f92-41a3-958a-593bf0b53015&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-master-next, full-part-2, 2026-09-07 (no patch under test): &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/385d5cab-9ea1-463c-ac25-d1368d2461e7" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/385d5cab-9ea1-463c-ac25-d1368d2461e7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The earlier &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19366" title="sanity-sec test_73: name  in CREAT is not short=a" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19366"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19366&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (empty name, user not registered on MDT0, closed as a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19429" title="sanity-sec test_35: FAIL: failed to clear changelogs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19429"&gt;LU-19429&lt;/a&gt;) has a different cause: here the CREAT record exists and its name is wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-65094-ps64-764e1394797c on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/65094" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65094&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
